<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Oparic – EIS</title><link>https://oparic.com/en/docs/eis/</link><description>Recent content in EIS on Oparic</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><atom:link href="https://oparic.com/en/docs/eis/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>EIS Extraction: CHI Instruments Data Preprocessing</title><link>https://oparic.com/en/docs/eis/extract_chi/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://oparic.com/en/docs/eis/extract_chi/</guid><description>
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="https://oparic.com/images/workflows/eis_extract_chi.png" alt="EIS Extraction: CHI Instruments Data Preprocessing" loading="lazy" /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have just received raw &lt;code&gt;.txt&lt;/code&gt; files exported from a CHI electrochemical workstation and are not sure where to begin, this workflow is the right starting point.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It automatically converts the raw EIS text into standardized tables (&lt;code&gt;*_eis.csv&lt;/code&gt;) and fills in the key columns needed for subsequent plotting and fitting. You do not need to rename columns manually or worry about minor differences between export formats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You Get&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="what-you-get"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#what-you-get" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;One &lt;code&gt;*_eis.csv&lt;/code&gt; file per sample&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unified fields: &lt;code&gt;freq_hz&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;z_real_ohm&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;z_imag_ohm&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;z_mod_ohm&lt;/code&gt;, &lt;code&gt;phase_deg&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Invalid data automatically removed (e.g., non-positive frequencies, empty values)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automatically sorted by frequency from high to low, ready for direct use in Nyquist/Bode/DRT workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Procedure&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="procedure"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#procedure" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Select the input folder&lt;/strong&gt;: choose the directory containing the raw CHI &lt;code&gt;.txt&lt;/code&gt; EIS files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The system traverses all &lt;code&gt;.txt&lt;/code&gt; files in the directory and processes them one by one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;On completion, an &lt;code&gt;xxx-eis-extract&lt;/code&gt; output folder is created alongside the input directory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If a file has an unexpected format, the system skips it with a warning and continues processing the remaining files.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Data Recognition Logic (Brief)&lt;span class="hx:absolute hx:-mt-20" id="data-recognition-logic-brief"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;a href="#data-recognition-logic-brief" class="subheading-anchor" aria-label="Permalink for this section"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The program first locates the &lt;code&gt;Freq/Hz&lt;/code&gt; header row, then automatically matches columns from common aliases:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequency column: &lt;code&gt;Freq/Hz&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;Frequency/Hz&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;f/Hz&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Real-part column: &lt;code&gt;Z'/ohm&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;Zreal/ohm&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;Z'/Ω&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Imaginary-part column: &lt;code&gt;Z&amp;quot;/ohm&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;Z''/ohm&lt;/code&gt; / &lt;code&gt;Zimag/ohm&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;From these, it computes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;span class="katex-display"&gt;&lt;span class="katex"&gt;&lt;span class="katex-mathml"&gt;&lt;math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"&gt;&lt;semantics&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mi mathvariant="normal"&gt;∣&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mi mathvariant="normal"&gt;∣&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msqrt&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mo mathvariant="normal"&gt;′&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;mo&gt;+&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mo mathvariant="normal"&gt;′&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mo mathvariant="normal"&gt;′&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mn&gt;2&lt;/mn&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msqrt&gt;&lt;mo separator="true"&gt;,&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mspace width="1em"/&gt;&lt;mi&gt;ϕ&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;=&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mi&gt;arctan&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo&gt;⁡&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mo fence="true"&gt;(&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mfrac&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mrow&gt;&lt;mo mathvariant="normal"&gt;′&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;mo mathvariant="normal"&gt;′&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;msup&gt;&lt;mi&gt;Z&lt;/mi&gt;&lt;mo mathvariant="normal" lspace="0em" rspace="0em"&gt;′&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/msup&gt;&lt;/mfrac&gt;&lt;mo fence="true"&gt;)&lt;/mo&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;/mrow&gt;&lt;annotation encoding="application/x-tex"&gt;|Z| = \sqrt{Z&amp;#x27;^2 + Z&amp;#x27;&amp;#x27;^2}, \quad \phi = \arctan\left(\frac{Z&amp;#x27;&amp;#x27;}{Z&amp;#x27;}\right)&lt;/annotation&gt;&lt;/semantics&gt;&lt;/math&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;span class="base"&gt;&lt;span class="strut" style="height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;∣&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.07153em;"&gt;Z&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mord"&gt;∣&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mrel"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="mspace" style="margin-right:0.2778em;